/* book: lead: A loaded point carries six stress numbers. A failure theory turns them into one number for comparison with a tension test. The maximum principal stress theory compares the largest normal stress with strength. The maximum principal strain theory compares the largest normal strain with yield strain. Both are simple, poor for ductile metals, reasonable for brittle castings. */
