/* book Worked example: Q: At an aluminium-alloy point σx = 100 MPa, σy = −40 MPa, τxy = 30 MPa, σY = 250 MPa, ν = 0.30. Find factors by both theories.
   1. σavg = (100 − 40)/2 = 30 MPa.
   2. R = √(70² + 30²) = 76.2 MPa.
   3. σ1 = 30 + 76.2 = 106.2 MPa; σ2 = 30 − 76.2 = −46.2 MPa; σ3 = 0.
   4. Rankine: 250/106.2 = 2.35.
   5. St Venant: ε1E = 106.2 + 0.3×46.2 = 120.0 MPa; ε2E = −46.2 − 0.3×106.2 = −78.0 MPa; ε3E = −0.3×60.0 = −18.0 MPa.
   6. Largest is 120.0 MPa; factor = 250/120.0 = 2.08. Strain theory governs.
   Answer: Factor 2.35 by maximum principal stress and 2.08 by maximum principal strain; strain theory governs. */
